 "issue": 1730,
 "issue_title": "Bug: quote date-like strings in schema_to_yaml",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n`schema_to_yaml()` emits date-looking string values without quotes, so YAML parsers can interpret them as timestamps instead of strings.\n\n## Why it matters\nSchema export should preserve data contract values exactly. If an allowed/default string such as `\"2026-05-28\"` is emitted unquoted, downstream YAML tooling may load it as a date object instead of a string, changing the schema semantics during round-trip or review.\n\n## Evidence\n- `arnio/schema_export.py`: `_emit_scalar()` quotes numeric-looking strings, booleans, null-like strings, strings with colons, and several special prefixes, but it does not quote ISO date-like strings.\n- Runtime probe on current main:\n  ```python\n  ar.schema_to_yaml({\"field\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"allowed\": [\"2026-05-28\"]}})\n  ```\n  produces:\n  ```yaml\n  fields:\n    field:\n      allowed:\n        - 2026-05-28\n      type: string\n  ```\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n1. Export a schema containing a string value that looks like `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n2. Load the YAML with a YAML parser that follows timestamp resolution rules.\n3. Observe that the scalar may become a date/timestamp instead of a string.\n\n## Expected behavior\nDate-looking string values should be quoted so they stay strings after YAML round-trip.\n\n## Actual behavior\n`schema_to_yaml()` emits `YYYY-MM-DD` strings as plain scalars.\n\n## Suggested direction\nExtend `_emit_scalar()` to quote date-like strings, at minimum values matching `^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$`. Add regression tests for allowed/default string values that look like dates.\n\n## References\n- `arnio/schema_export.py`\n- `tests/test_schema_export.py`\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1730",
 "pr": 1806,
 "pr_title": "fix: quote date-like strings in schema_to_yaml",
 "pr_body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nFixes #1730 \u2014 `_emit_scalar()` now quotes ISO date/datetime strings that YAML 1.1 parsers would otherwise resolve as timestamps.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n### `arnio/schema_export.py`\r\n- Added `_DATE_RE` compiled regex matching `YYYY-MM-DD` with optional time (`T` or space separator) and timezone suffix\r\n- Added `or bool(_DATE_RE.match(value))` to the `needs_quoting` condition in `_emit_scalar()`\r\n\r\n### `tests/test_schema_export.py`\r\n- `test_bare_date_in_allowed_is_quoted` \u2014 bare `2026-05-28` in `allowed` is emitted quoted\r\n- `test_iso_datetime_in_default_is_quoted` \u2014 ISO datetime string in `default` is quoted\r\n- `test_space_separated_datetime_is_quoted` \u2014 space-separated datetime is quoted\r\n- `test_yaml_roundtrip_preserves_date_string` \u2014 YAML loaded back has `str` type, not `date`\r\n- `test_non_date_strings_unaffected` \u2014 partial fragments like `05-28` and plain strings are unaffected\r\n- `test_date_with_time_zone_suffix_is_quoted` \u2014 datetime with timezone offset is quoted\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n\r\nThis PR is limited to the date-quoting fix and regression tests only. No other changes.",
